	affiliations = {Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Saveetha Engineering College, Tamil Nadu, Chennai, India},
	abstract = {This paper presents a unified smart-grid framework integrating solar forecasting, fault detection, and energy optimization using adaptive attention, federated learning, and quantum-inspired algorithms. The architecture combines TransDimNet with an Adaptive Multi-Resolution Attention Mechanism (AMRAM) to model temporal dependencies from solar irradiance, weather, and consumption data, improving solar prediction. A Bayesian Neural Network with Monte Carlo Dropout estimates Fourier-transformed features, while Federated Learning enables decentralized fault detection and predictive maintenance across grid components. Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning optimizes task prioritization, and Quantum-Inspired Neural Networks with a Decentralized Hierarchical Fuzzy Decision Framework perform dynamic load balancing and energy optimization. Validation on NREL, PVUSA, and GAN-generated datasets demonstrates superior performance. The framework achieves R<sup>2</sup> of 0.92, per-panel MAE of 0.245 kW, RMSE of 0.312 kW, and MAPE of 4.5%, outperforming existing hybrid models by 15–20% (p < 0.05). Fault detection attains 99% precision, 98% recall, and 99% accuracy, surpassing baselines by 3–5%. The QINN–DHFD combination delivers 98% grid efficiency and 20% reduction in energy loss under fluctuating conditions. These results establish the proposed framework as a robust, scalable solution for enhancing sustainability and resilience in next-generation renewable energy systems. © 2026 Elsevier Ltd. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies.},
